{
  "name": "Mesh Maps (raw)",
  "notes": "One file per baked map, named exactly as the Painter output preset names them today ($textureSet_$map with the standard map file labels). Outputs whose source map was not baked are skipped. Formats default to PNG, 16-bit for geometric maps (normals, position, height); the dialog's file-type and bit-depth overrides still win when set. The material alpha channel is labelled MaterialOpacity so it cannot overwrite the geometric Opacity map, which shares the same file label. Scene lighting outputs are 32-bit EXR so HDR irradiance survives. The two curvature variants (Principal, Direction) are written only when the Curvature row is set to that Output mode; the other two are skipped.",
